    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: CHANGES REQUESTED\n\nThe new exception class, the advice handler, and the private guard method all follow the existing patterns in this codebase cleanly (sibling exceptions like `DailyOwnerLimitException`, parallel `@ExceptionHandler` methods, and the `requireDailyCapacity`/`countOwnersRegisteredOn` family of private validators). The placement of the call in `createOwner` (reject before `resolveRegistrationDate` defaults it) is also sensible.\n\nThe one structural problem is where the method was inserted:\n\n- **Orphaned Javadoc / wrong-method documentation** (`OwnerRestControllerV1.java:207-234`). `rejectFutureRegistrationDate` was dropped *between* `requireDailyCapacity`'s Javadoc block and `requireDailyCapacity`'s body. The result:\n  - Lines 207-217 \u2014 the Javadoc describing the daily limit (`@throws DailyOwnerLimitException`, \"Rejects a create once ... owners already carry ... registration date\") \u2014 now sits directly above `rejectFutureRegistrationDate`, so the first doc comment a reader sees over the future-date guard describes a completely different rule.\n  - `requireDailyCapacity` (line 234) is now left with no Javadoc at all.\n  - Two `/** ... */` blocks are stacked back-to-back (lines 207-227), which is the visible symptom of the misplacement.\n\n  Fix: move `rejectFutureRegistrationDate` together with its own Javadoc (lines 218-232) out from between `requireDailyCapacity` and its doc comment \u2014 e.g. place it right after the `createOwner` method ends (before line 207) or after the complete `requireDailyCapacity` method \u2014 so each method sits directly beneath its own Javadoc.",
